Text:
The Reconciliator makes the desk open the files of some extensions with one program of the Fearless family, and show the icons of those extensions and of the windows of that program.
fearlessManager and the portable Fearless call the Reconciliator.
The 'identity' of the program calling Reconciliator.reconcile is the file name of the command of that program, without extension.
The 'Fearless family' is the set of the identities containing the text earless.
Two different versions, of fearlessManager or of the portable Fearless, never share an identity.
The 'setup' of an identity is every registry key and file that Reconciliator.reconcile writes for that identity.

Invariant:
Every Reconciliator.reconcile and every Reconciliator.eradicateAll holds, from start to end, the lock of the file fearlessAssociations.lock.

Define Reconciliator.eradicateAll:
A Reconciliator.eradicateAll deletes the setup of every identity of the Fearless family, with no check.

Implementation notes:
fearlessAssociations.lock is in the folder where the desk keeps the data of the programs the user runs: %LOCALAPPDATA% on Windows, $XDG_DATA_HOME on Linux, ~/Library/Application Support on macOS.
The code of the Reconciliator is the package fileAssociations of Commons.
